WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:05.670
Troubled Chinese developer Evergrande is exploring
a sale of its property-management firm as

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:09.990
part of a desperate-bid to sell-off assets
and raise much-needed cash.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:14.660
The firm owes more than 300 billion dollars
in unpaid bills.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:21.940
Beijing is worried about domestic unrest;
Foreign investors could be left empty-handed.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:27.640
There's a complete standstill on Evergrande's
construction sites.. workers have long left

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:32.369
long, many unsure if and how much they get
paid for their work.

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:37.190
But there might be an end in sight for the
real estate developer's crisis that has shaken

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:38.870
investors' confidence for weeks.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:44.920
Evergrande is selling a majority-stake in
its property management unit for more than

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:50.539
5 billion dollars, bringing in much needed
cash to carry on.

00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:59.770
"The goal is to separate the Evergrande Group
into three different units and ask the local

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:07.260
government to provide enough money for the
Evergrande Group to complete the projects

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.260
on hand.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:13.479
So that it can sell the completed flats to
the buyers.

00:01:13.479 --> 00:01:20.200
And the buyers can pay the Evergrande Group,
who in turn will pay off the contractors.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:27.690
So that, as far as the Chinese government's
concerned, this is the best way forward.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:35.810
And of course, in doing so, I think some creditors
will be hurt, mostly overseas creditors."

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:41.670
These creditors have known for a while that
their investment is at risk.. and still, another

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:47.210
trading week begins with markets worrying
about possible contagion and the fall-out

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.240
for China's entire economy.

